# A template of a script: the fixture harness runs it stepped
# (`fixture-test`; docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the gate runs a
# fixture"), with its setup (`Editor.Test.Fixture.Setup`): `note.txt` is
# copied into the file fake's model at `/fixture/note.txt`, which `@FILE@`
# stands for, and the run is against the config in `../config/`, of which
# it loads nothing. It has no expected file: the run must leave the model's
# copy holding the bytes of `note-expected` (`e`, an edit, `w` and `q`), and
# print no `commands:` line, which the `show` line after the quit would.

# `e` opens the file. The open is a job: `join` waits for its result, which
# makes the buffer and shows it. Without the wait the text below would be
# typed into the scratch buffer.
run ex
commit e @FILE@
key <Enter> Enter -
join

# `i` begins an insert at the file's start, and the committed text is typed
# text. `<Escape>` returns to normal state.
key i KeyI -
commit zero
key <Escape> Escape -

# `w` saves. The save is a job: `join` waits for its result, so the host's
# lines are in one order.
run ex
commit w
key <Enter> Enter -
join

# `q` quits: the buffer is saved, so the loop ends at the accept key. The
# `show` line after it is not run, so no `commands:` line is printed.
run ex
commit q
key <Enter> Enter -
show
